          "title": "You'll want to know: सफ़र",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सफ़र (safar) — \"a journey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic safar, 'travel', through Persian. The same root gives safīr, an ambassador — somebody sent out on a journey and expected back."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The inherited word is yātrā, from the Sanskrit root yā-, 'to go', and it leans toward pilgrimage. So a सफ़र (safar) is the road itself, while a yātrā is the road with a reason at the end of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: right now, the far day, a journey."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
