          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुलाक़ात (mulāqāt) — \"a meeting\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic mulāqāt, on laqiya, 'to meet', arriving through Persian. It covers everything from bumping into somebody on a street to a scheduled interview in an office."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It sits inside the ordinary parting line phir mulāqāt hogī, 'there will be a meeting again' — which is what फिर मिलेंगे says using inherited material instead of borrowed. Same farewell, two vocabularies, and a speaker can pick either without changing the meaning by a hair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: right now, the far day, a journey, setting out, a meeting."
            }
          ]
